+In this subsection, we time the deployed query path (cache probe, traversal of the compact tree arrays, region lookup, BF probe) with 10\% member queries, after checking that its FPs equal the main results bit for bit. Interestingly, the query cost is set mainly by the tree count. On COD and CAIDA the selected Gama and RA-family structures use 160 trees, a query takes 2.8--3.7\,$\mu$s, the model accounts for 94--98\% of it, and the cache adds less than 2\%. On Shalla \ra chooses 32 trees and answers in 548\,ns against 755\,ns for Gama's 48 trees. On URL 128\,KiB it chooses 48 trees against Gama's 16 and is 2.6$\times$ slower per query (728 against 280\,ns). On the traces, models of 1--4 trees take 28--79\,ns, and the cache probe makes \ra 5--39\,ns slower than Gama per query.
